      "text_raw": "The measured SNDR is\nshown in this slide. The\nSNR is the same, since the\ndistortion is very low up to\nthe reference voltage. This\nmeans that both the supply\nvoltage and the reference\nvoltage are 0.6 V. For an\ninput voltage of 0.6 V a\nptp\nSNDR is obtained of 78 dB.\nThis is quite impressive\nindeed.\nThe maximum signal band-\nwidth is about 24 kHz. It\nhas been realized in 0.35 mm\nCMOS and consumes only\n1 mW at 0.6 V.",
      "text": "The measured SNDR is shown in this slide. The SNR is the same, since the distortion is very low up to the reference voltage. This means that both the supply voltage and the reference voltage are 0.6 V. For an input voltage of 0.6 V a ptp SNDR is obtained of 78 dB. This is quite impressive indeed. The maximum signal bandwidth is about 24 kHz. It has been realized in 0.35 mm CMOS and consumes only 1 mW at 0.6 V."
